# Figure and coefficient table

`fig1.png` is the inspected 1400 × 700 pixel rendering (7 × 3.5 inches at 200 dpi). Use `fig1_caption.md` as the full caption and `../tables/coefficients.md` as the coefficient table. Both panels share series color/marker encodings; the residual panel uses initial OLS residuals even though the selected fit for B is WLS.

The generator consumes existing analysis outputs without fitting models. Input revision, hashes, selected result fields and software versions are recorded in `provenance.json`. Statistical computation lives in the analysis owner's `code/analysis.py`.

From the assembled delivery root (where `results/` is present), reproduce with:

```sh
python3 -m pip install -r figures/requirements.txt
python3 figures/generate.py --source . --analysis-revision 3f081036f482b788c52ec61c11d51d216824de52
```

For separate checkouts, set `--source` to the analysis repository root at that revision. If regenerating from a later analysis revision, pass its full revision identifier and review the new input hashes.

Inspection: opened the delivered PNG; both titles, axis labels, legends and extreme observations are visible, and line styles/markers distinguish the series. Read the generated caption, table, and provenance. Generator assertions verify matching observation/residual coordinates and reconstruct supplied OLS residuals from supplied coefficients to detect mismatched inputs. Table entries use the estimate/lower/upper fields directly and round to three decimals. No confidence band is implied by the fitted lines. No third panel was added because the two-panel figure meets the page constraints and directly displays the required initial residual check.

